# Configurable top and bottom bars

## Model (`shared/.../Layout.kt`, mirrored in `editor/src/model/types.ts`)

- `TopBar`: `date` (default true), `wifi` and `battery` (default false), `height` (null is 48 dp, clamped 32–120), `clockWidth` (percent of the screen width; null is `min(350, 42%)`, clamped 15–60), `background` / `clockBackground`.
- `Screen.navBar`: `show` (default true), `height` (null is 102 dp, or 66 dp under 600 dp wide, clamped 48–160), `labels` (`both` | `icons` | `text`), `layout` (`spread` | `center` | `fill`), colours `background`, `line`, `active`.
- `Screen.drawer`: `style` (`off` | `modal`), `side` (`start` | `end`), `width` (null is `Grid.MODAL_DRAWER` 300 dp, clamped 200–480), colours `background`, `active`. `ScreenValidator` keeps `navBar.show` true while the drawer is `off`, so the pages and Settings stay reachable. Unsupported saved styles fall back to `off`. `store.open()` also normalizes unsupported styles and restores the bottom bar before saving the initial editor snapshot.
- Colour fields take a theme role, a pastel key, or `#RRGGBB` / `#AARRGGBB`. The server resolves them with `DocContext.paint()` in `FreeForm.kt`.
- Defaults match the original look, so old layouts load unchanged. `TopBar.validated()` and `NavBar.validated()` clamp values. `navBar` is optional in TypeScript; `store.open()` sets `navBar ??= {}` before the saved copy, so opening an old screen is not a change.

## Grid math (keep Kotlin and TypeScript in step)

- `Grid.spec(size, w, h, topBar, navBar)` takes bar heights in dp. `Grid.topBarHeight` and `Grid.navBarHeight` return 0 when the bar is hidden. `Grid.navBarHeight` uses the width-based default when height is null. The modal drawer takes no space from the grid. `suggest()` (used on adoption) still uses the defaults.
- `editor/src/model/grid.ts` mirrors it with `Math.fround`. Its `spec` takes `(size, w, h, topBar, nav)`.
- `tests/fixtures/grid_parity.json` is the shared answer key. Regenerate with `./gradlew :shared:test -PupdateFixtures` and review the resulting diff.

## Renderer (`ScreenRenderer.kt`)

- Top bar scale `k = (spec.topBar / Grid.TOP_BAR).coerceIn(0.7, 2)` multiplies the header text, the icons, the Back key (capped at `topBar - 6`) and the spacers. The date shows only when `date` is on and the screen is at least `Grid.NARROW` wide.
- A weather temperature entity draws `weatherStateIcon` for its current condition (the weather page’s coloured sun, cloud and rain). The condition is structural, so a change rebuilds the document. A temperature sensor keeps the blue thermometer.
- Bottom bar scale is the bar height against that width's default bar, so the defaults draw as before. `navArrangement()` picks the row arrangement. `fill` makes each button `width / count` wide; the other layouts use square buttons.
- `GridMockup.vue` repeats this sizing. Change the renderer and the mockup together. Sliders need `v-range` (see `editor-sliders-and-theme-preview-context.mdc`).
- Content that spans the page (free-form root, edge-to-edge panels, page photo, empty-page message) uses `spec.widthDp`, below the top bar and above the bottom bar. Full-screen dialogs (the lights dialog) use the whole screen.
- `navItems()` builds the bottom bar's buttons (visible pages, then Settings). `render/NavDrawer.kt` builds the native drawer metadata separately.
- Modal drawer: the menu key sits in the top bar on the drawer's side (`menuKey`), or in the page's top corner when the top bar is hidden (`floatingMenuKey`). It sends `_|set|drawer|1`. The Android player renders `ModalNavigationDrawer`, `ModalDrawerSheet` and `NavigationDrawerItem` in `PlayerNavigationDrawer.kt`; the remote document contains no drawer panel or scrim. `RenderedDoc.navigationDrawer` carries the title, visible page indices, localized Settings label, SVG icon paths, width, side and resolved theme colors through `ServerMessage.Document.navigationDrawer`. Drawer gestures update the same local integer; choosing a row uses the existing local page/Settings actions. The player suspends the drawer while overlays, dialogs or standby are shown. Metadata changes force a document send even when the remote bytes match.
- Player: `RemoteScreenState.withDrawerClosed()` runs on every `showPage` and on Settings. `onBack` closes an open drawer after an overlay and before going home.

